---
import GovLayout from '../../layouts/GovLayout.astro';
---
<GovLayout title="Money Laundering & Criminal Faction" description="Mechanics of the Criminal Faction, Money Laundering, and Police interactions.">
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <span class="govuk-caption-xl">Justice & Law Enforcement</span>
      <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Money Laundering & Criminal Faction</h1>

      <p class="govuk-body-l">
        Delivering illicit cargo allows players to launder money, entering the Criminal Faction and participating in an active cat-and-mouse game with law enforcement. 
      </p>

      <div class="govuk-warning-text">
        <span class="govuk-warning-text__icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
        <strong class="govuk-warning-text__text">
          <span class="govuk-warning-text__assistive">Warning</span>
          Participating in these activities will put you at risk of being arrested by the Police and having your cargo confiscated. Both Criminals and Police require a custom mod map to participate.
        </strong>
      </div>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Required Mod Installation</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        To properly participate as a Criminal or a Police officer, you must install the <a href="/mods/MoneyRun_P.pak" class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state">MoneyRun_P.pak</a> custom mod map.
      </p>
      <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
        <li>Download the mod pak: <strong><a href="/mods/MoneyRun_P.pak" class="govuk-link">Download MoneyRun_P.pak</a></strong></li>
        <li>Locate your Motor Town install directory.</li>
        <li>Place the downloaded <code>MoneyRun_P.pak</code> file inside the <code>Motor Town/MotorTown/Content/Paks/~mods/</code> folder (create the <code>~mods</code> folder if it doesn't exist).</li>
        <li>Restart your game client.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Money Laundering Mechanics</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Players can deliver "Money" cargo to designated illicit drop-off points. Completing these deliveries triggers the money laundering process:
      </p>

      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Treasury Cost:</strong> Money laundering deducts 20% of the laundered payment from the overall Treasury Fund, actively draining public reserves.</li>
        <li><strong>Criminal Record:</strong> Successfully laundering money gives you an active Criminal Record lasting for 7 days. Any subsequent money deliveries will extend this duration by another 7 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Player Tag:</strong> While you have an active criminal record, you will be assigned a <code>[C]</code> tag in-game. As you launder more money, your criminal tier will increase (e.g., <code>[C2]</code>, <code>[C3]</code>) with every $100,000 laundered.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Law Enforcement & Confiscation</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Players serving in the Police Faction are tasked with intercepting criminal activity. After delivering Money, you will enter a <strong>Wanted</strong> state — during which Police can arrest you and confiscate your illegal earnings.
      </p>

      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Wanted duration:</strong> Up to 5 minutes, slowing down when police officers are nearby.</li>
        <li><strong>Manual arrest:</strong> Officers use <code>/arrest</code> to arrest nearby suspects over a 3-second verification period.</li>
        <li><strong>Auto-arrest:</strong> A patrol system automatically arrests suspects who remain stationary near an officer for 5 seconds.</li>
        <li><strong>Confiscation:</strong> A percentage of your most recent Money delivery is seized, proportional to remaining Wanted time. The confiscated amount goes to the Treasury and the arresting officer.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="govuk-body">
        For full details on Wanted status, arrest mechanics, confiscation rates, and police progression, see the <a href="/justice/arrest-wanted" class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state">Arrest &amp; Wanted System</a> documentation.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</GovLayout>
